h all of the fractions  of seven  so how does this help us solve the  puzzle  well what we'll do is we'll go from  fractions to six digit numbers  so we'll just remove the fraction parts  and we now end up with the number 14 28  57 and all of these multiplications are  still valid  we'll now arrange these numbers into a  six by six table  and there you go  in every row there are six different  digits with no repeats and in every  column there are six different digits  with no repeats this is a latin square  abc def is equal to 14 28 57 and i'm  pretty sure this is the only solution to  this puzzle because this is the only six  digit cyclical number in decimals which  doesn't have a leading zero  but i leave it open to you if you can  find any other possibilities or prove  why this is the only possibility  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video  these math videos inspire and build  confidence for people around the world  and they've already gotten over a  hundred million views but the math  meaties never praise these videos and  they spread their negativity  let's be extra positive to cancel them  out  please help the cause by subscribing for  free to get the newest videos and  watching and sharing all of mind your  decisions videos  you can also email me a puzzle or math  topic presh mindyourdecisions.com  check out my books which are linked in  the video description and you can  support me on patreon to earn exclusive  rewards thanks for watching and thanks  for your positive support
 

